[0.125,"o","\u001b[H\u001b[3G($1,198.78) — no more manual file-by-file\u001b[45Gpass.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BVerified:\u001b[13G\u001b[38;5;153mnpm test\u001b[22G\u001b[39m(18\u001b[26Gpassing),\u001b[36G\u001b[38;5;153mnpm run typecheck\u001b[39m,\u001b[55Gand\u001b[59G\u001b[38;5;153mnpm run build\u001b[73G\u001b[39mall\u001b[77Gpass.\u001b[83GThe\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bchanges are\u001b[15Guncommitted.\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;5;246m✻\u001b[3GWorked for 1m 37s · done 6:45 PM\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;5;237m\u001b[38;5;246m❯ \u001b[38;5;231mI called Marta. These are the criteria for FB-112, approved: 1. \u001b[38;5;153minvoicer aging <file> \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;153m--by-customer\u001b[38;5;231m prints one row per customer who has overdue invoices: the customer's \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mname, what they owe in each bucket (1-30, 31-60, 61-90, over 90 days) and their total \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231moverdue. 2. The customer with the largest total overdue comes first. 3. A customer with\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mnothing overdue is not listed. 4. Without --by-customer, aging prints exactly what it \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mprints today. If you have built something different already, change it to this.\u001b[39m         \r\u001b[2B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;5;246m \u001b[3G\u001b[39mThink\u001b[9Gng for \u001b[1m16s\u001b[22m…\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m  ⎿  \u001b[39m\u001b[2m\u001b[3mThe approved criteria differ from what I built: --by-customer is an opt-in flag, and \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bwithout it the output must be exactly as today. I need to change the implementation. \r\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m\u001b[3mLet me review current state and redesign: - \u001b[38;5;153maging()\u001b[39m should probably still always \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bcompute customers? The CLI can decide. Criterion 4 says without flag, aging prints 